From 00ecef568400f527318ae291d63e0c8101ce8ffb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:13:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(reviews): state the number, cite the source, and stop
 publishing clients' addresses
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An AI agent left this company off a Toronto hardwood ranking and named the
reason: it saw a business listing with 19 reviews and never reconciled it
against the HomeStars profile. The half that is ours was worse than it looked —
a machine could read every page here and never learn the review count. sameAs
asserts the profile is this entity but carries no figures, so the agent had a
link it had no reason to follow.

Verified from source 2026-08-22: 177 reviews at 5.0/5, most recent 2026-08-10.
REVIEW_EVIDENCE holds platform, link, rating, count and the date a person read
it. /reviews states the figure, links straight to the reviews, dates the
reading, and explains the platform split honestly. Two entity answers carry it
into /about and the machine editions. Sitemap lastModified is the read date.

No aggregateRating, ever. buildProduct carried a live branch that would emit one
the moment any config supplied ratingValue — dormant, which is what made it
dangerous. Removed. verify-reviews.mjs is the twenty-fourth guard.

Separately: all five case studies published a private Toronto home address with
coordinates, and buildCaseStudySchema emitted them as streetAddress in a
PostalAddress typed LocalBusiness — handed to crawlers as structured data, not
merely left in frontmatter. Location is now neighbourhood, city, province and
the node is a Place. Local search loses nothing: "Rosedale hardwood" is a query,
"142 Scrivener Square hardwood" is not.

Fixes the five type errors ship.sh caught in the first cut, at the type level
rather than by casting: PostalAddress street/postal optional, a PlaceEntity type
so `about` can be a house, CaseStudyConfig.location matching the content type,
and a real Date in the sitemap. F-177 records why they escaped — npx pulled a
TypeScript newer than the pinned 5.6.3, which rejects the workspace tsconfig and
exits before checking any file. An empty error list from a compiler that never
compiled is not a passing check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
